examples.question_text:
A stone is launched to the right at $24\text{ m/s}$ and $30^{\circ}$ above the horizontal. Take right and up as positive.
Find its initial horizontal and vertical velocity components, then write its initial velocity vector in exact form.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.1,0);
\draw[black,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.46,2) node[midway,above left] {$24\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=30,radius=0.8];
\path (1.15,0.3) node {$30^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Use cosine for the horizontal component and sine for the vertical component. Both components are positive.
$\begin{aligned}\dot{x}(0)&=24\cos30^{\circ}\\&=12\sqrt{3}\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\dot{y}(0)&=24\sin30^{\circ}\\&=12\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\underset{\sim}{v}(0)=12\sqrt{3}\underset{\sim}{i}+12\underset{\sim}{j}\text{ m/s}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{mathred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.46,2) node[midway,above left] {$24\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[mathblue,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.46,0);
\path (1.73,-0.4) node[text=mathblue] {$12\sqrt{3}\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[mathred,thick,->] (3.46,0)--(3.46,2);
\path (3.46,1) node[right,text=mathred] {$12\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=30,radius=0.8];
\path (1.15,0.3) node {$30^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
A ball is thrown to the right from a window at $18\text{ m/s}$ and $40^{\circ}$ below the horizontal. Take right and up as positive.
Find its initial horizontal and vertical velocity components and write its initial velocity vector. Give numerical components to 2 d.p.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(4,0);
\draw[black,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.06,-2.57) node[midway,below left] {$18\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[black] (0.8,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=-40,radius=0.8];
\path (1.15,-0.38) node {$40^{\circ}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
The ball moves right and down, so the horizontal component is positive and the vertical component is negative.
$\begin{aligned}\dot{x}(0)&=18\cos40^{\circ}\\&\approx13.79\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\dot{y}(0)&=-18\sin40^{\circ}\\&\approx-11.57\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\underset{\sim}{v}(0)\approx13.79\underset{\sim}{i}-11.57\underset{\sim}{j}\text{ m/s}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\definecolor{mathblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{mathred}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.06,-2.57) node[midway,below left] {$18\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[mathblue,thick,->] (0,0)--(3.06,0);
\path (1.53,0.35) node[text=mathblue] {$13.79\text{ m/s}$};
\draw[mathred,thick,->] (3.06,0)--(3.06,-2.57);
\path (3.06,-1.3) node[right,text=mathred] {$-11.57\text{ m/s}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

(a) Use Pythagoras for the speed and the sizes of the components for the acute angle.
$\begin{aligned}V&=\sqrt{5^{2}+(-12)^{2}}\\&=13\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\theta&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{12}{5}\right)\\&\approx67.4^{\circ}.\end{aligned}$
The velocity is $13\text{ m/s}$ at $67.4^{\circ}$ below the horizontal, directed to the right.
(b)
$\begin{aligned}V&=\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+15^{2}}\\&=17\text{ m/s}.\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\alpha&=\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{15}{8}\right)\\&\approx61.9^{\circ}.\end{aligned}$
The launch velocity is $17\text{ m/s}$ at $61.9^{\circ}$ above the horizontal, directed to the left. The negative horizontal component determines the leftward direction.
